    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Across the whole packet, policy debate follows one dominant pattern shown by the cited source.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_a82b7b39c563658b\",\"quote\":\"I agree with the hon. Gentleman entirely. I was not making a criticism of the think-tank, which has done its best, but we all know from experience that all economic forecasting should be taken with a slight grain of salt. It is utterly beyond the capacity of either the Treasury or the most expert outside groups to predict with absolute confidence what the precise consequences will…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_eba8317656a0282e\",\"quote\":\"In 2016, the Defence Committee produced a unanimous report called ‘Shifting the Goalposts? Defence expenditure and the 2% pledge’. We had the Committee staff use all available sourcing to draw up a definitive table of what had been spent on defence by Britain as a proportion of GDP over the past 50 years.”}],\"\n    }],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"Contextual flattening; the source presents a highly specific, narrow interpretation of debate patterns, ignoring broader contextual factors and potential counterarguments.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely asserts a universal pattern of policy debate, obscuring the diverse and complex nature of political discourse.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The cited excerpts demonstrate a focus on specific data (defence spending) and expert opinions, not a generalizable pattern of policy debate across all areas. The evidence does not support the claim of a single dominant pattern.\"}\n    ],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The source material provides evidence against a broad claim of a single dominant pattern in policy debate. The excerpts highlight specific data and expert opinions, indicating a narrow focus rather than a universal pattern. The claim is therefore unsupported by the provided evidence.\"}",
